1
00:03:06,206 --> 00:03:12,206
A Bride for Christmas is a romance, comedy, tv
movie film directed by Gary Yates.

2
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:18,413
Bride-to-be Jessie Patterson calls off her third
engagement - during the ceremony!

3
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:24,620
She swears off serious relationships, until she meets
and is pursued by Aiden MacTiernan.

4
00:12:24,827 --> 00:12:30,827
Aiden, on the other hand, has bet his friends he is marriage material, and
can find a fiancé in the four weeks leading up to Christmas.

5
00:15:31,034 --> 00:15:37,034
When Jessie and Aiden begin to fall for each other, Jessie must decide if she is ready for serious
love, and Aiden must decide if his bet is worth risking his relationship with Jessie.

6
00:18:37,241 --> 00:18:43,241
Jessie, played by Arielle Kebbel.

7
00:21:43,448 --> 00:21:49,448
Mike, played by Sage Brocklebank.

8
00:24:49,655 --> 00:24:55,655
Matt, played by Peter Benson.

9
00:27:55,862 --> 00:28:01,862
Marcie, played by Jordana Largy.

10
00:31:02,068 --> 00:31:08,068
Patty, played by Chelsey Reist.

11
00:34:08,275 --> 00:34:14,275
Aiden, played by Andrew W. Walker.

12
00:37:14,482 --> 00:37:20,482
Corpse Bride (also known as Tim Burton's Corpse Bride) is a 2005 stop-motion animated musical Gothic fantasy film
directed by Mike Johnson and Tim Burton and written by John August, Caroline Thompson, and Pamela Pettler.

13
00:40:20,689 --> 00:40:26,689
Set in an English village, Corpse Bride stars Johnny Depp as the voice of
Victor, while Helena Bonham Carter voices Emily, the title character.

14
00:43:26,896 --> 00:43:32,896
An international co-production between the United States and United Kingdom, produced by Tim
Burton Productions and Laika Entertainment, and distributed by Warner Bros.

15
00:46:33,103 --> 00:46:39,103
Pictures, Corpse Bride is the first stop-motion feature film directed by Burton after previously
producing The Nightmare Before Christmas (1993) and James and the Giant Peach (1996).

16
00:49:39,310 --> 00:49:45,310
Corpse Bride drew inspiration from a 17th-century Jewish folktale, which Joe Ranft
introduced to Burton while they were finishing The Nightmare Before Christmas.

17
00:52:45,517 --> 00:52:51,517
Work on the film started in November 2003 while Burton was wrapping up Big Fish.

18
00:55:51,724 --> 00:55:57,724
His next live-action feature, Charlie and the Chocolate Factory,
was produced simultaneously with Corpse Bride.

19
00:58:57,931 --> 00:59:03,931
Production of the stop-motion animation feature took
place at 3 Mills Studios in London.

20
01:02:04,137 --> 01:02:10,137
It was shot with Canon EOS-1D Mark II digital SLRs, rather than the 35
mm film cameras used for The Nightmare Before Christmas.

21
01:05:10,344 --> 01:05:16,344
Burton immediately brought regular collaborators
Depp, Carter and Danny Elfman aboard.

22
01:08:16,551 --> 01:08:22,551
Corpse Bride is dedicated to executive producer Ranft, who
died a month before the film's release.

23
01:11:22,758 --> 01:11:28,758
Corpse Bride premiered at the 62nd Venice International Film Festival on September
7, 2005, and was released in theaters on September 23 in the U.S.

24
01:14:28,965 --> 01:14:34,965
and on October 13 in the U.K.

25
01:17:35,172 --> 01:17:41,172
to critical and commercial success.

26
01:20:41,379 --> 01:20:47,379
The film was nominated for Best Animated Feature at the 78th Academy Awards.

27
01:23:47,586 --> 01:23:53,586
The film explores themes of bet, wedding, christmas.

28
01:26:53,793 --> 01:26:59,793
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
